    "label": "library-update-request",
    "body": "## Additional context and logs\n\n`native-image run` fails for `org.hibernate:hibernate-core:6.1.0.Final`. The test suite has\nnever passed since it was added on 2026-07-28 by #9120, and it now fails in this repo's own\nweekly CI as well as in oracle/graal's weekly reachability-metadata workflow.\n\nResult is stable across all runs: **6 tests successful / 4 tests failed, 6 of 13 containers failed.**\n\n### Where it fails\n\n| Run | GraalVM | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| [`test-all-metadata` 31922018764](https://github.com/oracle/graalvm-reachability-metadata/actions/runs/31922018764) (2026-08-16), batch 62/85 `current-defaults` ([job 95103431722](https://github.com/oracle/graalvm-reachability-metadata/actions/runs/31922018764/job/95103431722)) | Oracle GraalVM 25.0.4+7.1 | `FAILED[native-image run][6.1.0.Final]` |\n| same run, batch 62/85 `current-defaults` (job 95103431737) | GraalVM for JDK latest-ea | failed |\n| same run, batch 62/85 `future-defaults-all` (job 95103431744) | GraalVM for JDK latest-ea | failed |\n| `test-all-metadata` 31290966511 (2026-08-09), 30730051023 (2026-08-02) | \" | failed |\n| [oracle/graal Weekly Reachability Metadata Tests 31984989117](https://github.com/oracle/graal/actions/runs/31984989117/job/95259476201) (2026-08-17) | GraalVM CE 25.3.4.1-dev (graal master) | failed |\n\nThe failure is not GraalVM-version-specific — it reproduces identically on released Oracle\nGraalVM 25.0.4 and on a dev build from graal master, under both `current-defaults` and\n`future-defaults-all`. Every other hibernate coordinate in the same runs passes, including\n`org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-core:6.1.1.Final`.\n\n### Root cause 1 — 4 of 6 dialect constructors are unregistered\n\n`metadata/org.hibernate/hibernate-core/6.1.0.Final/reachability-metadata.json` registers\n`<init>()` for exactly two dialects, `H2Dialect` and `SQLServerDialect` (condition\n`typeReached: org.hibernate.boot.registry.selector.internal.StrategySelectorImpl`).\n\n`HibernateDialectTest` is parameterized over six. The two registered ones pass; the four\nunregistered ones fail:\n\n```\norg_hibernate.hibernate_core.HibernateDialectTest > [1] org.hibernate.dialect.H2Dialect SUCCESSFUL\norg_hibernate.hibernate_core.HibernateDialectTest > [2] org.hibernate.dialect.MariaDBDialect FAILED\norg_hibernate.hibernate_core.HibernateDialectTest > [3] org.hibernate.dialect.MySQLDialect FAILED\norg_hibernate.hibernate_core.HibernateDialectTest > [4] org.hibernate.dialect.OracleDialect FAILED\norg_hibernate.hibernate_core.HibernateDialectTest > [5] org.hibernate.dialect.PostgreSQLDialect FAILED\norg_hibernate.hibernate_core.HibernateDialectTest > [6] org.hibernate.dialect.SQLServerDialect SUCCESSFUL\n```\n\n```\n=> org.graalvm.nativeimage.MissingReflectionRegistrationError: Cannot reflectively invoke\n   constructor 'public org.hibernate.dialect.MariaDBDialect()'. To allow this operation, add\n   the following to the 'reflection' section of 'reachability-metadata.json' and rebuild the\n   native image:\n\n{\n  \"type\": \"org.hibernate.dialect.MariaDBDialect\",\n  \"methods\": [\n    { \"name\": \"<init>\", \"parameterTypes\": [] }\n  ]\n}\n\n   com.oracle.svm.core.reflect.MissingReflectionRegistrationUtils.reportInvokedExecutable(MissingReflectionRegistrationUtils.java:111)\n   java.base@25.0.4.1/java.lang.reflect.Constructor.acquireConstructorAccessor(Constructor.java:101)\n   java.base@25.0.4.1/java.lang.Class.newInstance(DynamicHub.java:715)\n   org.hibernate.boot.registry.selector.internal.StrategySelectorImpl.lambda$static$0(StrategySelectorImpl.java:38)\n   org.hibernate.boot.registry.selector.internal.StrategySelectorImpl.resolveStrategy(StrategySelectorImpl.java:241)\n   org.hibernate.boot.registry.selector.internal.StrategySelectorImpl.resolveDefaultableStrategy(StrategySelectorImpl.java:181)\n```\n\nIdentical errors for `MySQLDialect`, `OracleDialect`, and `PostgreSQLDialect`.\n\n### Root cause 2 — `META-INF/persistence.xml` is not registered\n\n`AbstractHibernateTest.init` calls `Persistence.createEntityManagerFactory(\"StudentPU\", …)`.\nNothing registers `META-INF/persistence.xml`:\n\n- library metadata `6.1.0.Final` has a single resource entry, `glob: META-INF/services/org.hibernate.*`\n- the test's `src/test/resources/META-INF/native-image/reachability-metadata.json` registers\n  only the five entity classes plus `glob: logback.xml`\n- `build.gradle` does no resource detection\n\nSo the lookup returns nothing at run time, no persistence unit is found, and all six\n`*DialectHibernateTest` classes fail in `@BeforeAll`:\n\n```\nJUnit Jupiter:H2DialectHibernateTest\n  => jakarta.persistence.PersistenceException: No Persistence provider for EntityManager named StudentPU\n     jakarta.persistence.Persistence.createEntityManagerFactory(Persistence.java:86)\n     org_hibernate.hibernate_core.AbstractHibernateTest.init(AbstractHibernateTest.java:48)\n     org_hibernate.hibernate_core.H2DialectHibernateTest.init(H2DialectHibernateTest.java:9)\n     Suppressed: java.lang.NullPointerException\n       org_hibernate.hibernate_core.AbstractHibernateTest.close(AbstractHibernateTest.java:55)\n```\n\n(also `MSSQL`, `MariaDB`, `MySQL`, `Oracle`, `Postgres`. The suppressed NPE is a follow-on —\n`entityManager` is never assigned, so `close()` dereferences null.)\n\nNote this one fails **silently**: unlike the reflection case there is no\n`MissingResourceRegistrationError`, just an empty result surfacing three layers up as a\nHibernate error, which makes it considerably harder to diagnose from the log alone.\n\nThe passing sibling `org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-core:6.1.1.Final` registers exactly this\nresource in its test metadata and passes:\n\n```json\n\"resources\": [\n  { \"condition\": { \"typeReached\": \"jakarta.persistence.Persistence\" },\n    \"glob\": \"META-INF/persistence.xml\" }\n]\n```\n\n### Why the metadata is this thin\n\n`6.1.0.Final` was not seeded from its predecessor. Comparing the committed files:\n\n| | `6.0.0.Final` (passing) | `6.1.0.Final` (failing) |\n|---|---|---|\n| reflection entries | 350 | **4** |\n| resource entries | 14 | **1** |\n| dialect constructors | all 6 | **H2 + SQLServer only** |\n| `META-INF/persistence.xml` | ✅ | ❌ |\n| `hibernate.properties` | ✅ | ❌ |\n| Hibernate DTDs / XSDs | ✅ | ❌ |\n\n#9120's own body reports the same collapse: *\"Metadata entries: 9 — Previous library version\nmetadata entries: 542.\"*\n\nThe same PR also flipped `metadata/org.hibernate/hibernate-core/index.json` so that\n`6.1.0.Final` is now the `latest` entry for `org.hibernate:hibernate-core`. The impact is\ntherefore not limited to this test suite — every consumer resolving metadata for that\ncoordinate now gets the near-empty version instead of the 542-entry `6.0.0.Final` one.\n\n### Minimum fix\n\n1. Add `<init>()` for `MariaDBDialect`, `MySQLDialect`, `OracleDialect`, and `PostgreSQLDialect`\n   to the library metadata, under the same `typeReached: StrategySelectorImpl` condition as the\n   two existing dialect entries.\n2. Register `META-INF/persistence.xml` in the test-side metadata, matching `6.1.1.Final`.\n3. Preferably: reseed `6.1.0.Final` from `6.0.0.Final` and regenerate, rather than patching the\n   two symptoms — the remaining ~340 dropped entries are latent failures for anything exercising\n   more of the library than this test suite does.\n4. Re-run the `native-image run` stage before merging. See the companion Forge issue for why\n   that gate did not run.\n\nRelated: #9119 (coverage follow-up, still open), #9120 (the PR that introduced this).\n\n## System information\n\n- **GraalVM version:** Oracle GraalVM 25.0.4+7.1 (also reproduced on GraalVM for JDK latest-ea and GraalVM CE 25.3.4.1-dev)\n- **Operating system:** Linux\n- **CPU architecture:** AMD64 (x86-64)",
